From 8b1d6b6b1375d67a0077974b5c7c79d75944a605 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:31:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 070/108] gpu: shader cache self-repair, live FXAA switch for
 the game's settings, compile threads off the game's cores, safer transfer
 skips

- Shader storage files the app can read but not write (copied in by adb or a file
  manager) are rewritten as the app's own copy instead of disabling the storage for
  the run (a shell-owned .xpso disabled the whole cache for a play session).
- lr_set_post_effect plugin export: the game's Settings > Anti-Aliasing (Off / FXAA /
  FXAA extreme) now reaches the renderer, through an atomic the GPU thread reads at
  the swap (CallInThread's queue isn't safe from guest threads).
- Android: pipeline creation threads run at nice 10 and may use every core but the
  slowest cluster (the app pins all threads to the middle cluster; compile bursts
  competed with the game's threads there).
- Overwrite cut-outs: no cut-out under face culling or a non-solid polygon mode, no
  constant-depth record with polygon offset.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h b/include/rex/graphics/command_processor.h
